From a7702f50edf71e2816066817863fa73ac3ddbca1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arc-moe <arc-moe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:03:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sycl: a native pack's cache slots lie in reverse, so the
 prompt path's loan is in the arena's first 4 GiB

The prompt path borrows the last expert-cache slots for its buffers (--prefill-borrow). On one 10-15 GB arena
they sat 7-11 GB in, and the oneMKL GEMMs of the batched prompt (kernels this build does not compile, so
-ze-opt-greater-than-4GB-buffer-required does not reach them) computed garbage there from layer 0's first
projection on: every prompt of ~1K tokens or more came out NaN ("!!!!", token 0), with the router sending
every token to the same 10 experts. The engine's own kernels read the same memory fine.

ExpertCache lays sized slots out last-first (STRATA_CACHE_TAIL_LOW=0: as before): device_slot and
slot_offsets give the addresses, slot_ends the sizes the loan is priced with, device_base the device plan's
base and lend_base(first) the loan's lowest address. Slot order, sizes and every rule over slot indices are
unchanged. Uniform-slot caches (the S2 kernels address base + slot * blob) and --vram-elastic keep the old
layout.

The batched prompt also checks its last residual row (40 KB, once per prompt): a non-finite one refuses the
request with a reason instead of answering "!!!!" (STRATA_PREFILL_NAN_CHECK=0: off).
